			OrangeButterfly.DisplayName: Orange Butterfly
			Bomber.DisplayName: Bomber
			Wheelie.DisplayName: Wheelie
			Batafire.DisplayName: Batafire

			MarxTownie: {
				DisplayName: Marx
				Census.SpawnCondition: Defeat a Pre-Hardmode Kirby boss OR enter Hardmode, and then wait for a rift to appear

				Dialogue: {
					DInitial: Hello! I've seem to have gotten lost in this strange new world! Will you keep me company? I can help you learn about my people, too! From one friend to another!
					D1: Why does your world's food taste so nasty? The only thing good here is the residue of whatever comes out at night!
					D2: Everyone has been billowing out of some weird star-shaped rifts into this place. It's a little annoying how many people I recognize.
					D3: Got a question? Glad to answer!
					D4: This world gives me a mixed feeling of fear and paranoia... it's great!
					D5: I can tell you anything that will help you along your way! After all, what are friends for... if not to be used?
					DDownedWOF: Wow! Seeing that guide disintegrate into ashes was... bad. Very bad. Yes.
					DPrePlant: Ever since those souls were released I've been thinking up a way to use them for our own benefit! My plan will be done soon...
					DPreMarx: Y'know, I think I've been a great friend helping you through all this. Maybe it's time you help me for once? Just gotta hear me out...
					DDefeat: So... about that... I guess I'm not quite me when I'm hungry!
					DPostMarx: Sorry about that fight... I was feeling a little hangry, is all!
					DPreMoonLord: I can feel cosmic horrors are loomimg above us... just the usual.
					DPreMoonLord2: I feel a powerful presence at the dungeon beckoning incomprehensible evil... not again.
					DLunarPillars: Unknowable entities invading from outside? Took them long enough.
					DPostMoonLord: Well, we're still here. With no way to get home... Got an interdimensional portal gun, or something?
					DMoon: What a cool moon!
					DShutTheHellUp: Everything is so strange in this... new world... Frankly, it's quite hard to adapt to this... forgotten land.
					DKirby1: All the monsters of this world would stand no chance against... him...
					DKirby2: Friend? Every world has its two-faced frauds, so don't let betrayal get to you, okay?
					DKirby3: ...Where is he?... He could be anywhere...
					DKirby4: Have you ever heard of a Galactic Nova? No? Okay, nevermind.
					DKirby5: That starboard is pissing me off.
					DReference: Friend! You gotta do SOOOOMMMMTHAAAAAYYYYYNNG!
					DMarxolor: What!? Do I look like a traitor to you!?
					#vvv Transformation mod reference
					DKirbyTransformation: Friend, appearances aren't everything, so I will help you no matter what! Even if you transform yourself into a horrific, abominable creature!
					#vvv Only appears with wotg enabled
					D1Hater: Look, I get you 'appreciate' her, but that Soylent character seems a little suspicious to me... especially her warp star...
					D1Hater2: What!? Soylent is gone!? Aw... don't worry about it, friend. I'm still here!
					DRift: Ah, things are finally looking up around here.
					DAOEDowned: Aaaaand everything sucks, again.
					DNamelessDowned: You beat God? Big whoop. I know a guy who does that every Tuesday.
				}

				Help: {
					HStarbits: Don't underestimate my guys! They carry with them their burning wishes to make a name for themselves! Though defeating them releases these wishes as tiny starbits! Perfectly usable for your own purposes!
					HWeapons: When my guys were brought here, they scurried all over the place! Try searching around! You might get something handy from them! Like a weapon to slay even more of them!
					HBosses: If there's something our worlds have in common, is that really powerful foes lurk in every corner! Surely some were carried here, too! Defeat them and earn some REAL valuable goodies!
					HWhispyWoods: Hey! Have you heard of Whispy Woods? Quite an infamous tree where I'm from! You could probably call him by combining an acorn with those starbits you might've been getting... and then make him into apple pie!
					HKracko: In our skies, a powerful cloud dominates with its power to work up a storm. I bet its juvenile form might've wandered into your skies! Try searching, and if that fails, then
					HKingDedede: I wonder if that fat slob of a king was brought into this world with everyone else... you need something precious that he'll hunt down a mile away, like one of his precious brooches! I've heard the dungeon might have what you need to make a copy...
					HMidbosses: Star rifts are what brought us all here, but they've stopped appering since! Hey, meteors are rumored to be associated with interdimensional capabilities! Perhaps you could cobble something together?
					HDreamMatter: Since the true form of this world has been revealed, I've been noticing some more of my guys being transported here. Something about them makes me think they have something more powerful than stars... like dreams!
					HRareStones: Hey, hey, hey! Ever heard of rare stones? They can only be found in between dimensions, so maybe pulling someone through a star rift might net you one!
					HEvoWeapons: With rare stones, you could upgrade some weapons to a fuller potential! Though these recipes aren't cheap, you seem like a skilled blacksmith!
					HNightmare: The Fountain of Dreams and the Star Rod, two artifacts of our world that make dreams come true! But with how much evil seems to arise at night in this world, would dreams only turn into nightmares? Only one way to find out!
					HHeartMatter: Love is something I find quite icky, but I think with some starbits, dream matter, and those ores of life energy in the jungle, you could make quite the valuable resource!
					HDarkMatter: There existed a dark force in our world, but it has mostly since been wiped out. Though I wonder if this world contains its own dark forces... Maybe you could try something with those souls of night?
					HRainbowSword: Hey! You've heard about a legend of a prismatic sword of light that can thwart all darkness forged with the many materials of this colorful world? Ridiculous, I know!
					HMarx: Hey, hey, hey! An awful evil slowly descends upon this world, but I have a plan: You know all those released ancient spirits? What if we were able to use them to our advantage? All you have to do is to find many souls and combine them with some heart matter to make the Sparkling Soul! Whaddya say?
					HZero: The Moon Lord sometimes makes me miss having an evil intergalatic force of darkness... but those luminous ores from that diabolical god might have enough darkness to resurect their ruler once more. Now THAT's a final battle I'd want to see!
					HPostZero: ...What? I don't have anything else to tell you. Friends are only useful for so long.
				}

				TownNPCMood: {
					Content: Everything is going accordingly... which means I'm happy!
					NoHome: You don't have a home for me? Oh, it's fine! I only promised to help you, is all...
					FarFromHome: How did I get here? Hey, friend? Do you mind taking me back home? I'd really appreciate it!
					LoveSpace: So much room to think! So much room to plan! I love it!
					DislikeCrowded: Now, friend, I enjoy a little compansionship, but it's a little hard to think in this environment.
					HateCrowded: Hey! I don't mean to be rude, but having too many patrons around makes it hard to plan... shoo them away already!
					LoveBiome: Such a beautiful, magnificent landscape bustling with activity! It really speaks to me, y'know?
					LikeBiome: A little chaos goes a long way... and this place has it!
					HateBiome: It's calm here... a little too calm here... It bores my senses!
					LoveNPC: Wow! Everyone hates {NPCName} so much! Their air of negativity is just admirable!
					LikeNPC: "{NPCName}'s penchant for destruction is awesome! I love a little chaos!"
					DislikeNPC: Why does {NPCName} prefer to help rather than hurt? You won't need help if you can hurt everyone around you!
					HateNPC: I hate {NPCName}! Every year, he gives me stupid, black, tasteless rocks! Even that puffball does a way better job with gifts than him!
					LikeNPC_Princess: "{NPCName}'s personality makes me gag... but she also gives me food, which is always appreciated!"
					Princess_LovesNPC: "{NPCName} may seem shifty, but as long as you keep him fed he'll always be a wonderful ally!"
				}

				Leave: Marx has escaped!
			}

			MarxTownieDown.DisplayName: Suspicious Looking Jester

			MarxPrelude: {
				DisplayName: Marx

				Dialogue: {
					1: It worked! I can't believe it worked!
					2: I got you to take me in, trust me as an ally, and you went and forged the Sparkling Soul...
					3: The ancient spirits are mine to control! Now I can establish this wacky world as my own!
					1Stranger: You thought I wouldn't notice you trying to obtain this?
					2Stranger: Pretending is my forte, and so is jumping in at the right moment!
					Rematch: You know how much I want that, so how about I just fight you already!
					Retry: You just don't know when to quit!
				}
			}

			MarxBoss.DisplayName: Marx

			PureDarkMatterRematch: {
				DisplayName: Dark Matter
				BossChecklistIntegration.EntryName: Zero
			}

			Bestiary: {
				BioSpark: An elite ninja that hides deep within the caverns, training to become stronger. Ambushes targets with a flurry of attacks.
				Birdon: This high-flying bird just loves to see how far can they fly! Got along very well with the harpies, and now they protect their blue feathery friends!
				BladeKnight: A fearless warrior constantly searching for a challenge to appease his desire for battle. Despite being an ametaur, anyways.
				Bomber: Don't let its cutesy, dinky appearance fool you. If it looks like a bomb, falls like a bomb, and explodes like a bomb... it's a bomb!
				BrontoBurt: Flutters through the air in a wave pattern. Will push others out of the way to keep on it's path.
				BroomHatter: Sweep, sweep, sweep! Must sweep the world clean! That's the monumental task this little guy puts on himself!
				BurningLeo: Burning Leos found comfort in the warm jungle, and now they scorch anyone who touches their land!
				Cappy: This shy creature keeps itself concealed with a mushroom like hat. Uncovering it reveals a face that doesn't look as cheery as they move.
				Chilly: Chillies found comfort in the cold tundra, and now they freeze anyone who touches their land!
				Kabu: A little wooden mound that slides around erratically in caves. Is rumored to carry a lot of wisdom.
				KnuckleJoe: Watch out! Knuckle Joe wants a challenge and you seem perfectly fit! They'll bombard you with a flurry of vulcan jabs and smash punches 'til you're down!
				OrangeButterfly: Life after death after life after death. The wheel of mortality never stops. It cannot stop, for the wheel, stopping means detaching from the cart, forever falling from existence. How can one cast judgement on that which cannot be judged? That is the dilemma this emissary of fate faces.
				ParasolDee: A waddle dee that likes to take its umbrella out for walks, even when it isn't raining.
				PlasmaWisp: A ghastly entity sparking high amounts of electricity and light. Tries to snuff out intruders of its domain.
				PoppyBrosJr: This happy little demolitionist loves to throw, toss, and hurl bombs! All while keep a wide grin on its face that never seems to wash off!
				Scarfy: A cute little face that stands out amongst the demons and flames, but only if you keep it that way!
				SirKibble: A fearless warrior that refuses to back out of a battle, even when the odds are stacked against them.
				UFO: Rarely some may see mysterious constructs floating around the atmosphere. They tend to open fire on suspicious life forms that get too close.
				WaddleDee: Simple minded wanderers that have no desire to fight. Although they can be quite the nuisance when you're in a hurry.
				WaddleDoo: The more dangerous cousin of the Waddle Dee. Shoots out electric beams whenever it feels threatened.
				Bonkers: A giant armored monkey that came from a strange star shaped rift, prepared to smash down on any threat that approaches with its hammer!
				MrFrosty: An icy beast that appeared in the tundra from a strange star shaped rift. Does its best to stamp out any threats with style and grace, or lack thereof.
				Batafire: When this fiery fiend appeared from the star-shaped rift it immediately found solace where it made sense the most: the only other places with bats and heat!
				Whispy: A tree that gained the unatural ability of sentience, and now has devoted its life to guarding it's brethren.
				Kracko: Kracko is a living cloud that has lingered in the sky since ancient times, and thus has mastered the art of thunder!
				KingDedede: The mighty-yet-greedy ruler of a distant castle! He loves to snack and show those who mistreat him the boot! Especially people who take his precious life-saving brooches!
				Nightmare: An evil wizard bent on spreading nightmares to all that can dream. Its magic can twist the mind and body of those who are cursed with it.
				DarkMatter: A mysterious monocular invader with a body as black as darkness itself. What hidden motives does it have descending upon this world?
				MarxTownie: A friendly face has appeared from a land of dreams to help you figure out his world's weird visitors! He's a little weird, himself, but there's nothing wrong with that... right?
				MarxBoss: A two-faced fiend with incredible magical abilities that used your trust (or curiosity) to secure an artifact that could've enabled him to rule all of Terraria... that was, until he got thwarted!
				Zero: The supreme ruler of all matter that is dark, reborn once more into another world through a ritual involving Cthulhu's fallen essence.
			}
		}

